invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh poly1305-avx2
reason: the last group multiplies lane 1 by r^6 and lane 2 by r^7, the
  powers the other lane's blocks are owed, so every block those two
  lanes held is off by one power of r and the tag is wrong for every
  update the kernel takes. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, and only an
  x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/poly1305_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under qemu-x86_64. The
  lane skips without docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than
  caught.

--- old
    const uint32_t *const last_first[4] = {of_r.r8, of_r.r7, of_r.r6, of_r.r5};
--- new
    const uint32_t *const last_first[4] = {of_r.r8, of_r.r6, of_r.r7, of_r.r5};
